     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the usual maximum:\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n1. **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum).\n2. **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n3. **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n4. **1,700 mg three times daily is intended.** If so, please confirm explicitly and I'll enter it with a note that you verified the dose."
      }
     ],
